      "id": "sol.amc-8-1987-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "One hour has \\(3600\\) seconds, so the computer does \\(10{,}000 \\times 3600 = 36{,}000{,}000\\) additions.\n\nThat is \\(36\\) million.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "There are \\(60 \\times 60 = 3600\\) seconds in an hour",
        "Multiply the rate \\(10{,}000\\) by the number of seconds in an hour"
